. do "20250729_220003_01tur0_h2.do"

. *****************************************************************************
> ***
. ****************** Example Do-File H2: #ManyDaughters Project ***************
> ***
. *****************************************************************************
> ***
. 
. * Authors: [REDACTED], [REDACTED]
. 
. * ============================
. * Setup *
. * ============================
. 
. *clear all
. version 18

. set maxvar 10000 // extend the maximum number of variables to 10,000


. *ssc install outreg2
. /*
> * CONFIGURE FILE PATHS *
> * the following code automatically sets paths based on where you saved the di
> stributed file-package on your system *
> if strpos("`c(pwd)'", "code") {
>     global ROOT "`c(pwd)'/.."
> }
> else {
>     global ROOT "`c(pwd)'"
> }
> global IN "$ROOT/data/raw" // folder, in which the original datasets are stor
> ed
> global DATA "$ROOT/data/derived" // folder for datasets
> global OUT "$ROOT/out" // folder for output (results, tables)
> */
. 
. * ============================
. * Data Preparation * 
. * ============================
. 
. * LOAD AND MERGE DATA *
. 
.         use "$IN/ppathl.dta", clear // use ppathl as a starting dataset
(SOEP-Core, v37 (EU Edition), doi:10.5684/soep.core.v37eu)

.         * Keep only measures that will be used in the analysis
.     keep pid syear sex gebjahr netto pop migback sampreg 

.         * Merge ppathl with datasets.
.         * pl contains all variables from the individual questionnaire
.         merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pl.dta", nogen keep(master matches) ke
> epusing(plh0258_h ple0008 plh0004)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

.         * biobirth contains information on fertility history
.         merge m:1 pid using "$IN/biobirth.dta", nogen keep(master matches) ke
> epusing(kidsex* kidgeb*)
(variable pid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(label sex already defined)
(label sex_EN already defined)
(label pid_EN already defined)
(label cid_EN already defined)
(label cid already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

.         * pgen contains user-friendly data on the individual level that are c
> onsolidated from different sources
.         merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pgen.dta", nogen keep(master matches) 
> keepusing(pgfamstd pgemplst pglabnet pglabgro pgbilzeit)
(variable syear was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

.         * bioparen
.         merge m:1 pid using "$IN/bioparen.dta", nogen keep(master matches) ke
> epusing(fsedu msedu)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

.         
.         label language EN // change language of the labels to English

. 
.         save "$DATA/h2_dataset.dta", replace // save merged dataset
file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/95%-sample/h2_dataset.dta saved

. 
. 
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
.         * 1. Only keep participants from private households
.         keep if inlist(pop,1,2)
(89,279 observations deleted)

.         * 2. Only keep respondents who completed the individual questionnaire
>  with household interview (with survey status between 10 and 15). These are a
> ll individuals 18 years and older.
.         keep if netto>=10 & netto<=15
(69,516 observations deleted)

.         * 3. Retain only respondents who had at least one child at any point 
> before or during the sample period.
.         rename kidgeb0* kidgeb* // Renaming the variables kidgeb01-kidgeb09 t
> o be kidgeb1-kidgeb9. This will be useful when using the loop "forvalues i(1)
> 19" later.

.     keep if syear>=kidgeb1 & kidgeb1>0
(144,084 observations deleted)

.         * Retain only respondents who declared the gender of at least one of 
> their children (some did not)
.         rename kidsex0* kidsex*

.         forvalues i=1(1)19{
  2.                 qui g kid_gender_declared`i'=1 if kidsex`i'>0
  3.         }

.         egen at_least_one_kid_gender = rowtotal(kid_gender_declared*)

.     keep if at_least_one_kid_gender>0
(119 observations deleted)

.         drop kid_gender_declared* at_least_one_kid_gender       

. 
. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES *
. sort pid syear

. 
.         * Generate dummy variable for respondents with at least one daughter 
> up to the year of the survey (1 if at least one daughter, 0 if not). The foll
> owing code also creates a variable that measures the total number of daughter
> s each participant has up to the year of the survey.
.         forvalues i=1(1)19{
  2.                 qui replace kidgeb`i'=. if kidgeb`i'>syear // If the ith c
> hild is born in year t, and the observation year is earlier than t, then the 
> variable kidgeb`i' (year of birth of the ith child) is left empty.
  3.                 qui replace kidsex`i'=. if kidgeb`i'>syear // If the ith c
> hild is born in year t, and the observation year is earlier than t, then the 
> variable kidsex`i' (gender of the ith child) is left empty.
  4.         }

.         g Having_Daughters=0

.         g Num_Daughters=0

.         forvalues i=1(1)19{
  2.                 qui replace Having_Daughters=1 if kidsex`i'==2
  3.                 qui replace Num_Daughters=Num_Daughters+1 if kidsex`i'==2
  4.         }

. 
.         * Left-leaning political preferences
.         g Political_Preference_Left=(-1)*plh0004 if plh0004>0 // We reverse t
> he variable so that higher values reflect a more left-leaning orientation.
(300,347 missing values generated)

.         
.         
.         * Generate controls
.         // Gender of the respondent
.         rename sex Gender

.         // Age of the respondent
.         g Age=syear-gebjahr

.         // Marital Status of the respondent
.         g Marital_Status=pgfamstd if pgfamstd>0
(1,570 missing values generated)

.         // Employment status
.         rename pgemplst Employment_Status

.         // Income (Net)
.         g Income_Net=pglabnet if pglabnet>=0
(150,526 missing values generated)

.         replace Income_Net=0 if pglabnet<0 & Employment_Status==5 // Income_N
> et is assumed to be zero for individuals who are not employed and who did not
>  declaire any income (pglabnet=-2)
(150,524 real changes made)

.         // Education in years
.         g Education_In_Years=pgbilzeit if pgbilzeit>=0
(4,733 missing values generated)

.         // Number of Children up to the observation year
.         g Num_Sons=0

.         forvalues i=1(1)19{
  2.                 qui replace Num_Sons=Num_Sons+1 if kidsex`i'==1
  3.                 }       

.         g Num_Children=Num_Daughters+Num_Sons

.         // Migraation background
.         rename migback Migration_Background

.         // Sample region
.         g Sample_Region=sampreg if sampreg>0
(22 missing values generated)

.         // Religion
.         g Religion=plh0258_h if plh0258_h>0
(271,572 missing values generated)

.         // Parents minimum education level      
.         g Parents_Min_Edu=min(msedu, fsedu) if fsedu>=0 & msedu>=0
(55,641 missing values generated)

.         // Current health
.         g Current_Health=ple0008 if ple0008>0
(452 missing values generated)

. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 *
.         * Verbal description of the model: Support_Gender_Equality = β₀ + β₁ 
> * Having_Daughters + Controls + ε 
.         
.         * We consider a: linear OLS regression
. 
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis (with robust s
> tandard errors) using Political_Preference_Left as dependent variable and the
>  dummy variable Having_Daughters as independent variable. 
.         reg Political_Preference_Left Having_Daughters Gender Age Marital_Sta
> tus Employment_Status Income_Net Education_In_Years Num_Children Migration_Ba
> ckground Sample_Region Religion Parents_Min_Edu Current_Health, vce(robust)

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =     14,637
                                                F(13, 14623)      =      57.41
                                                Prob > F          =     0.0000
                                                R-squared         =     0.0477
                                                Root MSE          =     1.5147

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |               Robust
Political_~t | Coefficient  std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
Having_Dau~s |  -.0005783    .028947    -0.02   0.984    -.0573181    .0561615
      Gender |   .3817334   .0268476    14.22   0.000     .3291087    .4343581
         Age |   .0009962    .001101     0.90   0.366    -.0011619    .0031544
Marital_St~s |   .0177946   .0094073     1.89   0.059    -.0006448     .036234
Employment~s |   .0039847   .0086967     0.46   0.647    -.0130618    .0210312
  Income_Net |  -8.20e-07   8.61e-07    -0.95   0.341    -2.51e-06    8.68e-07
Education_~s |   .0958386   .0046767    20.49   0.000     .0866715    .1050056
Num_Children |   .0014277   .0134248     0.11   0.915    -.0248867    .0277421
